    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c989b71d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image juxtaposes a historical photo of Ku Klux Klan members with text claiming they killed 3,446 Black people over 86 years, then contrasts it with a claim that since 2016, 1,891 Black people were killed by other Black people in Chicago alone. The intent is to provoke outrage by equating historical systemic racial violence with contemporary Black-on-Black violence, implying that the latter is somehow comparable or even worse. This comparison is harmful as it minimizes the historical and systemic nature of white supremacist violence against Black communities and attempts to deflect attention from institutional racism by framing contemporary violence as an internal Black issue. The meme uses the visual of the KKK to evoke fear and historical trauma, then uses the statistic to create a misleading and inflammatory comparison that can incite racial division and hostility. The overall intent is to manipulate perception by creating a false equivalence between two vastly different types of violence, thereby potentially justifying or downplaying systemic racism.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_bdae0928"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_cd3dbfd5",
      "@type": "TextualMaterial",
      "instance_name": "text_chunk",
      "label": "top_text",
      "description": "the ku klux klan killed 3446 blacks in a span of 86 years",
